# Test: a committed `pppoe` edit reaches the running access concentrator: a
# changed ac-name is announced, an added access interface answers PADI, and a
# removed one stops answering.
#
# VALIDATES: pppoe.Subsystem.Reload applies the diff live. After the SIGHUP
#            reload, a PADI on the newly configured veth-bng2 gets a PADO
#            carrying the new AC-Name (RFC 2516 Section 5.2).
# VALIDATES: a PADI on veth-bng, which the reload removed, gets no PADO.
# PREVENTS: the accepted-and-ignored reload. Reload returned nil and did
#           nothing, so the commit succeeded while the AC kept answering with
#           the boot configuration on the boot interface until a restart.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: with Reload a no-op, veth-sub2 never gets a PADO (the driver
# fails "after the reload: no PADO on veth-sub2 ..."), and veth-sub keeps
# answering AC-Name=ze-before.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw
option=netns-link:name=veth-bng:peer=veth-sub
option=netns-link:name=veth-bng2:peer=veth-sub2

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
pppoe {
    enabled true
    ac-name ze-before
    interface veth-bng {
    }
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
pppoe {
    enabled true
    ac-name ze-after
    interface veth-bng2 {
    }
}
EOF_CONF2

option=env:var=ze.log.pppoe:value=info

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture pppoe/reload before=veth-sub:ze-before after=veth-sub2:ze-after silent=veth-sub:timeout=90s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: before reload veth-sub answered AC-Name=ze-before
expect=stdout:contains=OK: after reload veth-sub2 answered AC-Name=ze-after
expect=stdout:contains=OK: after reload veth-sub left PADI unanswered
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
